{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.AppendixSurreals.HyperrealLimitTransfer","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.HyperrealLimitTransfer","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.AppendixSurreals.SurrealLimitTransfer","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.Real.Hyperreal"],"declarations":23,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.HyperrealTransfer.surrealLimitTransferHyperreal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.HyperrealTransfer.surrealLimitTransferHyperreal","kind":"def","line":294,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/HyperrealLimitTransfer.lean#L294-L303","doc":"**`SurrealLimitTransfer ℝ*`.**  A `def` for the same reason\n`surrealFieldHyperreal` is: it is only as meaningful as the carrier it sits on. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.HyperrealTransfer.isClose_iff_isSt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.HyperrealTransfer.isClose_iff_isSt","kind":"theorem","line":286,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/HyperrealLimitTransfer.lean#L286-L292","doc":"`IsClose` at `ℝ*` is exactly Mathlib's `IsSt`.  This is the bridge lemma, and it\nis the reason §3 is cheap: `IsInfinitesimal (x - ofReal r)` unfolds to\n`∀ ε > 0, |x - r| < ε`, which is `Hyperreal.isSt_iff_abs_sub_lt_delta`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.HyperrealTransfer.surrealFieldHyperreal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.HyperrealTransfer.surrealFieldHyperreal","kind":"def","line":253,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/HyperrealLimitTransfer.lean#L253-L274","doc":"**The independence witness.**  `ℝ*` satisfies every `SurrealField` axiom, with a\nbirthday that is not Conway's.\n\n⚠ **`def`, deliberately not `instance`.**  Promoting this to a global instance would\nmake every `SurrealField`-generic theorem in the corpus silently apply to `ℝ*` under a\ntwo-valued birthday.  It is used only via `attribute [local instance]` in §3, where\nnothing being proved mentions `birthday`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.HyperrealTransfer.omega_gt_natCast","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.HyperrealTransfer.omega_gt_natCast","kind":"theorem","line":249,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/HyperrealLimitTransfer.lean#L249-L251","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.HyperrealTransfer.flatBirthday_ofReal_le_omega","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.HyperrealTransfer.flatBirthday_ofReal_le_omega","kind":"theorem","line":244,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/HyperrealLimitTransfer.lean#L244-L247","doc":"**`birthday_ofReal_le_omega` holds**, for the same bounded-by-`1` reason. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.HyperrealTransfer.flatBirthday_avg_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.HyperrealTransfer.flatBirthday_avg_le","kind":"theorem","line":229,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/HyperrealLimitTransfer.lean#L229-L242","doc":"**`birthday_avg_le` holds — and holds vacuously.**\n\n`Basic.lean` documents this axiom as \"exactly Conway's `{L | R}` recipe\" and as\n\"genuinely independent of `birthday_add_le`\".  Under a birthday bounded by `1` the\nright-hand side is `≥ 0 + 1 = 1` no matter what, so the axiom constrains nothing.\nThat is the sharpest form of the defect: the axiom carrying the most design\ncommentary in `Basic.lean` is the one this model satisfies with the least effort. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:thm:birthday-axioms-underdetermine","label":"thm:birthday-axioms-underdetermine","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/birthday-axioms-underdetermine.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.HyperrealTransfer.flatBirthday_add_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.HyperrealTransfer.flatBirthday_add_le","kind":"theorem","line":217,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/HyperrealLimitTransfer.lean#L217-L227","doc":"**`birthday_add_le` holds.**  The only case with any content is `x + y ≠ 0`, and\nthere at least one of `x, y` is nonzero, so the right-hand side is already `≥ 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.HyperrealTransfer.one_le_nadd_flatBirthday","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.HyperrealTransfer.one_le_nadd_flatBirthday","kind":"theorem","line":205,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/HyperrealLimitTransfer.lean#L205-L215","doc":"`1 ≤ flatBirthday x ♯ flatBirthday y` whenever `x` and `y` are not both zero. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.HyperrealTransfer.flatBirthday_neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.HyperrealTransfer.flatBirthday_neg","kind":"theorem","line":202,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/HyperrealLimitTransfer.lean#L202-L203","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.HyperrealTransfer.flatBirthday_omega_lt_omega0","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.HyperrealTransfer.flatBirthday_omega_lt_omega0","kind":"theorem","line":194,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/HyperrealLimitTransfer.lean#L194-L200","doc":"**The two-valued model is not Conway's birthday**, stated as an inequality that\ndoes not depend on knowing `flatBirthday`'s definition: an element strictly above every\nnatural number is assigned a birthday strictly below `ω`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.HyperrealTransfer.flatBirthday_omega","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.HyperrealTransfer.flatBirthday_omega","kind":"theorem","line":190,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/HyperrealLimitTransfer.lean#L190-L192","doc":"Conway: `birthday ω = ω`.  Here: `1`, and `1 ≠ ω`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.HyperrealTransfer.flatBirthday_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.HyperrealTransfer.flatBirthday_two","kind":"theorem","line":186,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/HyperrealLimitTransfer.lean#L186-L188","doc":"Conway: `birthday 2 = 2`.  Here: `1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.HyperrealTransfer.flatBirthday_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.HyperrealTransfer.flatBirthday_one","kind":"theorem","line":178,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/HyperrealLimitTransfer.lean#L178-L178","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.HyperrealTransfer.flatBirthday_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.HyperrealTransfer.flatBirthday_zero","kind":"theorem","line":176,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/HyperrealLimitTransfer.lean#L176-L176","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.HyperrealTransfer.flatBirthday_le_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.HyperrealTransfer.flatBirthday_le_one","kind":"theorem","line":169,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/HyperrealLimitTransfer.lean#L169-L174","doc":"`flatBirthday` is bounded by `1` — the fact every axiom below leans on. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.HyperrealTransfer.flatBirthday","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.HyperrealTransfer.flatBirthday","kind":"def","line":162,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/HyperrealLimitTransfer.lean#L162-L167","doc":"**The two-valued candidate birthday**: everything nonzero is born on day 1.\n\nThis is transparently *not* Conway's birthday — under Conway, `birthday 2 = 2`,\n`birthday (1/2) = 2`, `birthday ω = ω`.  The point of the lemmas below is that\n`Basic.lean`'s axioms cannot tell the difference. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.HyperrealTransfer.hyperrealOfReal_strictMono","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.HyperrealTransfer.hyperrealOfReal_strictMono","kind":"theorem","line":158,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/HyperrealLimitTransfer.lean#L158-L159","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.HyperrealTransfer.hyperrealOfReal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.HyperrealTransfer.hyperrealOfReal","kind":"def","line":150,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/HyperrealLimitTransfer.lean#L150-L156","doc":"The real embedding `ℝ →+* ℝ*`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.HyperrealTransfer.tendstoReal_le_of_eventuallyLE'","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.HyperrealTransfer.tendstoReal_le_of_eventuallyLE'","kind":"theorem","line":128,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/HyperrealLimitTransfer.lean#L128-L140","doc":"**Limit comparison through the hyperreal order**, unconditionally.\n\nThe whole argument is routed through a single inequality at `ω` plus the\nmonotonicity of the standard part — the \"inequality → nonstandard statement → real\ninequality\" round trip, with no conjecture class in the statement.\n\n(The strict-inequality collapse is visible here too: `ofSeq a < ofSeq b` is perfectly\ncompatible with `L = M`, which is why only `≤` survives.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.HyperrealTransfer.ofSeq_le_ofSeq_of_eventuallyLE","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.HyperrealTransfer.ofSeq_le_ofSeq_of_eventuallyLE","kind":"theorem","line":119,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/HyperrealLimitTransfer.lean#L119-L126","doc":"**Eventual domination transfers to the hyperreal order.**  This is the one step\nthat uses `Nat.hyperfilter_le_atTop`, and it uses it in the *only* direction that is\navailable. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.HyperrealTransfer.st_ofSeq_of_tendstoReal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.HyperrealTransfer.st_ofSeq_of_tendstoReal","kind":"theorem","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/HyperrealLimitTransfer.lean#L113-L117","doc":"**Limits are computed by `st ∘ ofSeq`.**  The unconditional `ℝ*` form of\n`standardPart_evalOmega_of_tendstoReal`. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:thm:hyperreal-limit-transfer","label":"thm:hyperreal-limit-transfer","md":"quantum-observable-universe/appendix-surreals/hyperreal-limit-transfer.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.HyperrealTransfer.isSt_ofSeq_of_tendstoReal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.HyperrealTransfer.isSt_ofSeq_of_tendstoReal","kind":"theorem","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/HyperrealLimitTransfer.lean#L107-L111","doc":"The ω-evaluation of a convergent sequence has the limit as its standard part —\nin Mathlib's `IsSt` form. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.HyperrealTransfer.tendsto_atTop_of_tendstoReal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.HyperrealTransfer.tendsto_atTop_of_tendstoReal","kind":"theorem","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/HyperrealLimitTransfer.lean#L94-L100","doc":"The kernel's ε–N convergence implies Mathlib's `Tendsto … atTop (𝓝 L)`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}